    "content": "<p class=\"black-color mb-30\">\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Dark patches or discoloration around the mouth can be frustrating, making your skin appear uneven or dull. Known as perioral <a href=\"https://www.drdivyasharma.com/Struggling-with-Pigmentation/\">hyperpigmentation</a>, this condition affects many people, especially those with medium to darker skin tones. The good news? With care from a dermatologist, consistent skincare, and medical treatments, you can brighten your skin and enjoy a more even complexion.</p>\n\n<h2>Understanding Pigmentation Around the Mouth</h2>\n\n<p>Pigmentation in this area often happens due to excess melanin production—the pigment that colors your skin. Dr. Divya Sharma, senior dermatologist at her Whitefield clinic in Bangalore, explains several common causes:</p>\n\n<p>Sun Exposure: The mouth area often misses sunscreen, leading to darkening from UV rays.</p>\n\n<p>Hormonal Changes: Pregnancy, birth control pills, or thyroid imbalances can trigger melasma-like pigmentation around the mouth.</p>\n\n<p>Post-Inflammatory Hyperpigmentation (PIH): Dark spots left after acne, waxing, or irritated skin.</p>\n\n<p>Vitamin B12 Deficiency: This can show up as pigmentation on lips and surrounding skin.</p>\n\n<p>Lifestyle Factors: Smoking, stress, and lack of proper sun protection worsen discoloration.</p>\n\n<p>Dr. Divya highlights that identifying what causes your pigmentation is key to successful treatment.</p>\n\n<h3>Dermatologist-Approved Treatments by Dr. Divya Sharma</h3>\n\n<p>At her clinic, Dr. Divya Sharma offers personalized treatment plans tailored to Indian skin types prone to pigmentation. Recommended treatments usually include:</p>\n\n<h3>Topical Solutions:</h3>\n\n<p>Vitamin C and kojic acid serums brighten skin and counter sun damage.<br>\r\nNiacinamide prevents pigment transfer for a more even tone<br>\r\nPrescription creams like azelaic acid or hydroquinone <a href=\"https://www.drdivyasharma.com/Treat-Pigmentation-Effectively/\">reduce stubborn spots safely</a>.<br>\r\nRetinoids improve cell turnover and skin texture gradually.</p>\n\n<p>Chemical Peels:<br>\r\nMild AHA or lactic acid peels gently exfoliate, removing pigmented layers and encouraging fresh skin growth over sessions.</p>\n\n<p><br>\r\nLifestyle Adjustments:</p>\n\n<p>Protect your skin daily with SPF 30 or higher, especially around the mouth.</p>\n\n<p>Avoid rubbing or harsh scrubbing.<br>\r\nConsume vitamin-rich foods and maintain hydration.<br>\r\nQuit smoking and manage stress for better skin health.</p>\n\n<h3>When to See a Dermatologist</h3>\n\n<p>If pigmentation has lingered for months or worsens despite home care, <a href=\"https://www.drdivyasharma.com/Causes-and-treatment-of-hyperpigmentation/\">consult a dermatologist </a>like Dr. Divya Sharma for diagnosis and tailored treatment. Professional guidance ensures safe, visible improvements and prevents side effects.</p>\n\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n\n<p>Pigmentation around the mouth may take time to reduce, but with personalized, dermatologist-backed care and persistence, you can achieve clear, radiant skin. According to Dr. Divya Sharma, it’s about restoring natural, healthy, and balanced skin—not chasing quick fixes.</p>\n\n<p><br>\r\n </p>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Dark patches or discoloration around the mouth can be frustrating, making your skin appear uneven or dull. Known as perioral <a href=\"https://www.drdivyasharma.com/Struggling-with-Pigmentation/\">hyperpigmentation</a>, this condition affects many people, especially those with medium to darker skin tones. The good news? With care from a dermatologist, consistent skincare, and medical treatments, you can brighten your skin and enjoy a more even complexion.</p>\n\n<h2>Understanding Pigmentation Around the Mouth</h2>\n\n<p>Pigmentation in this area often happens due to excess melanin production—the pigment that colors your skin. Dr. Divya Sharma, senior dermatologist at her Whitefield clinic in Bangalore, explains several common causes:</p>\n\n<p>Sun Exposure: The mouth area often misses sunscreen, leading to darkening from UV rays.</p>\n\n<p>Hormonal Changes: Pregnancy, birth control pills, or thyroid imbalances can trigger melasma-like pigmentation around the mouth.</p>\n\n<p>Post-Inflammatory Hyperpigmentation (PIH): Dark spots left after acne, waxing, or irritated skin.</p>\n\n<p>Vitamin B12 Deficiency: This can show up as pigmentation on lips and surrounding skin.</p>\n\n<p>Lifestyle Factors: Smoking, stress, and lack of proper sun protection worsen discoloration.</p>\n\n<p>Dr. Divya highlights that identifying what causes your pigmentation is key to successful treatment.</p>\n\n<h3>Dermatologist-Approved Treatments by Dr. Divya Sharma</h3>\n\n<p>At her clinic, Dr. Divya Sharma offers personalized treatment plans tailored to Indian skin types prone to pigmentation. Recommended treatments usually include:</p>\n\n<h3>Topical Solutions:</h3>\n\n<p>Vitamin C and kojic acid serums brighten skin and counter sun damage.<br>\r\nNiacinamide prevents pigment transfer for a more even tone<br>\r\nPrescription creams like azelaic acid or hydroquinone <a href=\"https://www.drdivyasharma.com/Treat-Pigmentation-Effectively/\">reduce stubborn spots safely</a>.<br>\r\nRetinoids improve cell turnover and skin texture gradually.</p>\n\n<p>Chemical Peels:<br>\r\nMild AHA or lactic acid peels gently exfoliate, removing pigmented layers and encouraging fresh skin growth over sessions.</p>\n\n<p><br>\r\nLifestyle Adjustments:</p>\n\n<p>Protect your skin daily with SPF 30 or higher, especially around the mouth.</p>\n\n<p>Avoid rubbing or harsh scrubbing.<br>\r\nConsume vitamin-rich foods and maintain hydration.<br>\r\nQuit smoking and manage stress for better skin health.</p>\n\n<h3>When to See a Dermatologist</h3>\n\n<p>If pigmentation has lingered for months or worsens despite home care, <a href=\"https://www.drdivyasharma.com/Causes-and-treatment-of-hyperpigmentation/\">consult a dermatologist </a>like Dr. Divya Sharma for diagnosis and tailored treatment. Professional guidance ensures safe, visible improvements and prevents side effects.</p>\n\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n\n<p>Pigmentation around the mouth may take time to reduce, but with personalized, dermatologist-backed care and persistence, you can achieve clear, radiant skin. According to Dr. Divya Sharma, it’s about restoring natural, healthy, and balanced skin—not chasing quick fixes.</p>\n\n<p><br>\r\n </p>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t</p>\r\n                </div>\r\n                <!-- event-details - end -->\r\n            </div>",
